  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d95f71226bf26bc4caed6a0458a3b538, type: 3}
  m_Name: Lesson 23 Question 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: True or false - The Holy Spirit led the writers of the Bible to document
    God's truth?
  answers:
  - False
  - True
  - ..........
  - ..........
  correctAnswerIndex: 1
  discussionAnswer: Scripture is inspired, or "breather out" by God. Peter explained
    that "no prophecy was ever produced by the will of man, but men spoke from God
    as they were carried along by the Holy Spirit" (2 Peter 1:21). The Holy Spirit
    led the writers to write exactly what God wanted them to write.
